1
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:54,520
He dribbled past him!

2
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:56,920
Jeez, what a lousy shot.

3
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,640
I'd do better out there myself.

4
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:01,440
How many chicken racks have you had?

5
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:03,440
Are you watching the game or keeping watch?

6
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:05,800
However many I eat, it's not on your dime.

7
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:09,080
I've been watching all morning. My eyes are going blind.

8
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:10,800
I don't even want to scold you two.

9
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:12,440
You can't take Xing San's word seriously.

10
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:13,440
Boss!

11
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:15,000
Another plate of chicken hearts.

12
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:15,960
Coming right up.

13
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:19,160
Go easy on those. They're high in cholesterol.

14
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:21,040
I ordered them for you. You are what you eat.

15
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:24,040
Then save them for you and my brother-in-law.

16
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:25,480
Perfect late-night snack for you two.

17
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:33,520
What are you doing?

18
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:34,840
Hold onto this sketch. I've got an errand to run.

19
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:36,640
How big an ass needs that much paper?

20
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:37,680
Am I keeping you from wiping your mouth?

21
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:39,560
Didn't you say no bathroom breaks?

22
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:42,320
So strict with others, so lenient with yourself.

23
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,880
How old am I? How old are you?

24
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,360
Can you show some respect for the elderly?

25
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:47,280
I'm on insulin shots and still toughing it out here.

26
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,320
-No bathroom here, right?
-Not here.

27
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:50,040
-That way.
-Get going. Don't crap your pants.

28
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:52,440
Make yourself useful. Keep your eyes peeled.

29
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:54,320
A lazy donkey always needs to piss at work.

30
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,440
Pass it! Don't you know how to pass?

31
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:09,400
Hey, don't clear this table.

32
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:11,320
-I'll be right back.
-Sure thing.

33
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:20,000
(Sports Lottery Super Lotto)

34
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:28,800
Ah, forget it.

35
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:30,680
Play these numbers.

36
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:41,920
You still want change?

37
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,480
Why not just grab some scratch cards?

38
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:45,000
What's the fun in those?

39
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:46,360
There's no skill involved.

40
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:47,520
Those are quick.

41
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:49,080
One flip and you know.

42
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:50,440
Give me one, then.

43
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:52,600
Here. The money.

44
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:53,680
Knock yourself out.

45
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:00,160
-Did anyone win today?
-Yeah.

46
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:01,840
-How many?
-Two.

47
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:03,560
Why didn't you say so earlier?

48
00:04:03,640 --> 00:04:06,280
It's struck twice already, no third time.
My luck's run out.

49
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:08,120
It's all down to luck anyway.

50
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:10,240
-You're hustling me here. Honestly...
-Well...

51
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:13,720
-Boss, ten yuan's worth for me.
-Sure.

52
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:16,320
-Uh... all quick picks.
-Quick picks?

53
00:04:16,399 --> 00:04:17,760
What's the fun in quick picks?

54
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:19,760
Isn't that just wasting money?

55
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:22,320
The machine's theirs.
Why would it side with you

56
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:23,600
and let you win?

57
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:27,480
Come on, you pick your own numbers.
How many times have you won?

58
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:29,320
And how many times have you won with quick picks?

59
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:31,360
Man, how many times have I won?

60
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:32,360
Let me tell you.

61
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:33,560
My car, my apartment...

62
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:35,640
All bought with quick-pick winnings. Believe it?

63
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:36,720
Keep bragging.

64
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:38,280
Hey, bragging's tax-free anyway.

65
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:40,280
Buddy,

66
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,800
let me give you a piece of advice.

67
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:43,080
Before you buy a lottery ticket,

68
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:45,560
fill your heart with peace and devotion.

69
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:48,080
What kind of attitude is that?

70
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:50,920
You don't know a kindness when you see one.

71
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,280
He really won't budge, soft or hard.

72
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:54,480
Print me a quick pick too.

73
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:20,960
To the traffic police.

74
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,160
Then get another cab.

75
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:24,200
I'm not taking fares today.

76
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:25,480
You don't have a choice.

77
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:26,760
Move it.

78
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:30,400
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

79
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:32,920
You know damn well what I'm doing.

80
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,120
-I've got things to do.
-You don't want your cab anymore?

81
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:37,120
-Trying to run?
-Bro, what are you doing? Hey...

82
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:38,080
Not short on cash, huh?

83
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:39,400
Bro, easy! Wait...

84
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:42,040
Your apartment and car were bought
with quick picks, right?

85
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:43,440
-Bro...
-Don't you struggle with me.

86
00:05:43,520 --> 00:05:44,760
Don't tussle. I've had training, you know.

87
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:45,960
The two of us, over a quick pick?

88
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:47,240
Is this really necessary?

89
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:49,360
-Cut the crap.
-I'm telling you, my arm was hurt in a fight.

90
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:50,480
-Don't move...
-It's injured! Easy!

91
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:53,160
You... what are you... hey, is this necessary?

92
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:54,520
Calling in backup, over this little thing?

93
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:56,720
You flatter yourself.
Why would I need backup to handle you?

94
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:58,120
Ever heard of mixed martial arts?

95
00:05:58,200 --> 00:05:59,640
Are we even in the same weight class?

96
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:01,400
I could crush you just by sitting on you.

97
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:03,000
Done squirming yet?

98
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:05,760
-Go ahead.
-Found him. Get over here.

99
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:10,600
Bro, you can stop digging.

100
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:11,960
There's nothing in my pockets.

101
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:13,760
I haven't had a single fare today.

102
00:06:14,520 --> 00:06:16,840
He thinks we're highway robbers.

103
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:21,360
So... so you're not robbing me?

104
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:23,120
Let me give you a piece of advice.

105
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:25,320
In a bit, answer whatever we ask. Got it?

106
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:29,040
Just keep that peace and devotion
in your heart, and you'll be fine.

107
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:32,440
Fellas, did you maybe grab the wrong guy?

108
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:34,560
I've got no beef with you. What is this?

109
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:36,880
No mistake.

110
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:38,560
You're exactly who we want.

111
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:41,480
Do I even know you?

112
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:42,680
The cornfield.

113
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:44,840
You ran pretty fast.

114
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:46,080
Got scared after you hit someone?

115
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:47,920
Hey, what do you mean?

116
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:49,400
When did I ever hit anyone?

117
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:50,840
Let me jog your memory.

118
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:54,160
The morning of October 20th,
you were driving this cab,

119
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:57,280
with fake plates: Hua AW357F.

120
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:58,320
Ring a bell?

121
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:01,640
Bro, come on, I'm just an unlicensed cabbie.

122
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:03,240
I'm no gangster.

123
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:05,200
Who would I dare hit? Me, run someone over?

124
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:07,480
Young man, the three of us aren't cops.

125
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:09,440
Hey, even if you said you were cops,

126
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:10,520
I'd have to believe it first.

127
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:11,840
-Why so chatty?
-What are you doing?

128
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:14,720
-No rough stuff. Ask nicely.
-Just answer what we ask, all right?

129
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:15,840
What's going on?

130
00:07:16,320 --> 00:07:17,400
Here's the thing.

131
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:18,880
We're not after you.

132
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:20,680
We're after the person you hit.

133
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:22,120
I'll say it one more time.

134
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:23,200
I didn't hit anyone.

135
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:25,840
Kid, why are you so stubborn?

136
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:28,360
If we had no evidence,
why would the three of us come for you?

137
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:31,640
You hit someone. That's settled fact.

138
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:34,080
Just tell us who you hit,

139
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:35,640
and we'll let you go right away.

140
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:38,720
Playing peaceful now, huh?

141
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:40,360
Easy with him.

142
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:43,760
-Biao, do it.
-All right then.

143
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:45,280
Don't pull the knife.

144
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,840
What knife? We can't go committing crimes.

145
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:48,240
-I'll cripple him.
-Bro, look at yourselves...

146
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:49,240
at your age.

147
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:50,600
Why would we go that far?

148
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:55,320
Won't talk, huh?

149
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:56,960
What do we do?

150
00:07:58,600 --> 00:07:59,920
Turn him in.

151
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,760
You're done for. This time you're really done for.

152
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:04,200
(PAUSED)

153
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:06,840
All right, thank you for supporting our work.

154
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:09,120
Oh, comrade, no need for thanks.

155
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:10,240
Police and people are one family, after all.

156
00:08:10,320 --> 00:08:11,960
Then let's not stand on ceremony.

157
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,560
When can I drive my cab out of here?

158
00:08:13,640 --> 00:08:15,680
-Go to the accident division for the paperwork.
-Sure.

159
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:18,400
Comrade, he didn't just fake the plates.
There's definitely more to it.

160
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:20,800
Please find out who he hit.

161
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:22,000
Don't you worry.

162
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:23,840
Hit-and-run means criminal charges, guaranteed.

163
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:25,600
Everything will be investigated thoroughly.

164
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:26,800
-We'll notify you once we have results.
-Good.

165
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:28,000
-Head on back now.
-All right.

166
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:29,400
-Let me know when you have results.
-Sure.

167
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:30,680
The name's Wang Xiang.

168
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:32,600
-"Xiang," as in "resounding."
-Sure...

169
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:34,840
Wang Xiang.

170
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:38,440
What are you really after?

171
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:47,320
Another plate of lamb.

172
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:49,240
What seafood do you have?

173
00:08:49,760 --> 00:08:51,480
-We have squid.
-Add a squid.

174
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:53,440
Don't order so much. We can't finish it all.

175
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:55,560
It's not much. Add a bellflower root salad.

176
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:57,680
Go ahead. We'll order more if needed.

177
00:08:57,760 --> 00:08:58,720
Sure thing.

178
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:09,240
Since you two won't get things started,
I'll propose the first toast.

179
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:10,640
How can we start without drinks?

180
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:11,880
How could there be no drinks?

181
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,160
Here, brother-in-law.

182
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:16,560
This meal is mainly to treat Captain Ma.

183
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:17,480
That's right.

184
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,280
If it weren't for you,

185
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:20,920
I wouldn't have gotten my cab back so fast.

186
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,320
No need to thank me.

187
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:24,600
Once the matter was cleared up,
naturally the cab was returned.

188
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:26,120
No, you can't put it that way.

189
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:27,720
Without you,

190
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:29,160
it wouldn't have gone so smoothly.

191
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:30,360
-Right.
-Am I right?

192
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:32,760
-Come on then.
-Cheers.

193
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:41,680
Here, eat up.

194
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:46,720
Aren't you going to propose one?

195
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:48,840
Nothing you want to say?

196
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:52,880
Go on, say something.

197
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:55,640
To Captain Ma.

198
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:56,920
I don't want to hear that.

199
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,240
Say something else.

200
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:02,680
Like what?

201
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:05,240
Honestly, what should I say?

202
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:09,520
Brother-in-law, Captain Ma is one of us.

203
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:11,040
Just say whatever's on your mind.

204
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:14,520
What I'd say isn't exactly solid.

205
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:15,800
Better not say it.

206
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:17,280
If you won't drink, let's eat.

207
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:18,640
Then can I say it?

208
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:22,120
Well, who did that fake-plate car hit?

209
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:25,040
You two went through all this trouble.

210
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:27,360
What do you want with him?

211
00:10:33,920 --> 00:10:35,640
Stop keeping it under wraps.

212
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:36,920
It's pointless.

213
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:46,600
Since the conversation's come this far,

214
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:48,720
let me tell you something interesting.

215
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:53,360
The person that fake-plate car hit...

216
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:56,720
is the one who got Yang'er killed.

217
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:59,760
That's a bit interesting, no?

218
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:03,680
Interesting.

219
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:05,840
Go on then.

220
00:11:12,560 --> 00:11:13,640
We got him on camera.

221
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:28,560
There's no face here.

222
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:30,680
How can you tell it's him?

223
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:33,000
Look.

224
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:36,640
You didn't believe me back then.

225
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:38,960
And you still don't believe me now.

226
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:40,480
So what's the point of me talking?

227
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:42,360
What do you expect me to believe?

228
00:11:42,880 --> 00:11:44,040
Wang Xiang,

229
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:46,920
this business with Yang'er
has driven you obsessed.

230
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:49,960
He's lost it, and you're losing it with him?

231
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:51,000
No, Captain Ma.

232
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:53,200
-It's mainly my brother-in-law...
-No, if you got to the bottom of this,

233
00:11:53,280 --> 00:11:54,840
would I still be obsessed?

234
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:56,360
Wang Yang committed suicide.

235
00:11:56,440 --> 00:11:57,960
I told you that 18 years ago.

236
00:11:58,040 --> 00:11:59,360
It wasn't suicide.

237
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:01,240
I know my own son.

238
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:03,640
His killer was Fu Weijun.

239
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:04,800
Here we go again.

240
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:05,880
Haven't I told you?

241
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:07,280
When you were at the railway tracks,

242
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:09,320
Fu Weijun had already been caught by us.

243
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:10,600
Then how did he get to the tracks?

244
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:12,360
Exactly. It wasn't him.

245
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:18,480
You don't have to believe me,

246
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:20,440
but when we arrested him,

247
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:22,000
so many pairs of eyes were watching.

248
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:23,000
Could they all be wrong?

249
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:24,360
Which is why you're wrong.

250
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:26,560
You were wrong 18 years ago.

251
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:27,600
Everyone, calm down.

252
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:28,640
Don't you say a word.

253
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:29,640
Just tell me this:

254
00:12:29,720 --> 00:12:31,000
Fu Weijun is in prison now.

255
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:32,720
How could he have gotten out
and been hit by a car?

256
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:34,880
Then tell me, how did my son die?

257
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:36,440
Why are you shouting at the two of us?

258
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:38,160
Do you think we cops just talk nonsense all day?

259
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:41,040
We rely on evidence, not imagination.

260
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:42,720
Is this imagination? Isn't this evidence?

261
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:44,520
-How is this not evidence?
-This what?

262
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:47,200
No face in it. If this isn't imagination,
then what is it?

263
00:12:47,280 --> 00:12:48,440
What is this?

264
00:12:48,520 --> 00:12:50,200
-Just tell me...
-Nothing, it's fine...

265
00:12:50,280 --> 00:12:51,400
It's nothing. Sorry about that.

266
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:53,320
It's fine...

267
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:54,840
Sorry, folks...

268
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:56,120
A little too much to drink.

269
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:59,200
Both of you, calm down.

270
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:01,040
How old are you two combined?

271
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:02,240
What are you doing?

272
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:04,640
Take it home, whatever it is.

273
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:07,080
Wang Xiang, you need to understand

274
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:09,640
what I'm saying.

275
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:12,160
You dwell on this day after day.

276
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:13,880
Anyone would lose their mind.

277
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:16,240
Whose family hasn't lost someone?

278
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:20,720
My wife died of cancer last year.

279
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,080
So what? Should I stop living?

280
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:24,160
Is that the same thing, Captain Ma?

281
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:27,560
Your wife died of illness.

282
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:29,880
She died in a hospital, in a bed.

283
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:31,680
That's dying of old age.

284
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:34,440
My son wasn't even 20,
and he died in the water.

285
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:36,720
How can I not think about it every day?

286
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:07,000
Calm down.

287
00:14:17,680 --> 00:14:19,000
Is the rest still coming?

288
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:20,680
Coming? Who cares?

289
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:21,680
Can we return it?

290
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:24,080
-Sir, we can't take dishes back.
-Then pack it up...

291
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:18,120
What's with that attitude of yours?

292
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:20,040
I came here demanding some accountability,
you hear me?

293
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:21,000
My attitude has been perfectly fine.

294
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:21,960
-Pay up.
-What kind of attitude is this?

295
00:15:22,040 --> 00:15:23,880
-The pay-compensation kind. Pay up.
-But...

296
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:24,960
You...

297
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:26,480
Well, isn't that Sister Xu?

298
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:28,200
What's that on your... did you get a stye?

299
00:15:28,280 --> 00:15:30,360
Bullshit. What stye?

300
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:32,080
I had two perfect double eyelids.

301
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:33,800
Look what your wife did to me.

302
00:15:33,880 --> 00:15:35,000
Now one's single and one's double.

303
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:37,120
Once I finish your other eye, we're done, right?

304
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,920
Right. You fix my eye properly

305
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,280
and don't charge me for it.

306
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:41,760
Call it a freebie.

307
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:43,400
You think I'd still let you touch me?

308
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:44,680
If you blind me, whose fault is that?

309
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:47,160
It's cold out here. Come in and talk.

310
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:49,320
What's wrong? Back-alley clinic scared of being heard?

311
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:51,000
Scared of what? Everything I do is legit.

312
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:52,840
Legit, my ass. You got a license?

313
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:53,840
I'm in the process of getting one.

314
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:54,880
So that's a no.

315
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:57,360
I'll have it any day now. It's coming through.

316
00:15:57,440 --> 00:16:00,280
This is practicing medicine without a license, you know that?

317
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:02,720
Xu-jie, let's be fair here.

318
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:05,040
A procedure like yours would run six grand at a real hospital, no?

319
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:07,840
At my place, I gave you two grand with ten percent off.

320
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:09,320
You get what you pay for.

321
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:10,600
Don't you know that much?

322
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:12,640
So I was cheap, and I deserve this? Is that it?

323
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:14,080
I never said that. Listen here—

324
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:15,360
-Enough...
-Hey! Get your hands off!

325
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:17,240
Stop wasting breath on her. Let's call the cops.

326
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:19,120
No... call... call what? Don't call.

327
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:21,480
We've got a problem, let's work it out.

328
00:16:22,480 --> 00:16:23,880
I'll pay whatever's fair, fair and square.

329
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:26,600
You think this is about the money?

330
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:29,520
If you two are willing to pay up,

331
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:31,040
-150 grand.
-How much?!

332
00:16:32,040 --> 00:16:34,160
150 grand? You're shaking us down!

333
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:35,520
Who are you calling a scammer?

334
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:36,840
I'm calling YOU scammers. So what?

335
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:38,320
Is 150 grand too much?

336
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:40,000
If I go blind,

337
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:41,600
you're doing time, got it?

338
00:16:41,680 --> 00:16:42,680
Enough.

339
00:16:42,760 --> 00:16:43,960
Come on, sis.

340
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:45,960
We're all old Hualin Steel folks, right?

341
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:47,880
We can talk anything over nicely.

342
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:50,520
Do me a solid here, knock it down some.

343
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:51,760
How's ten grand sound?

344
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:53,360
Here, take the phone. Call the cops.

345
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:55,000
Who do you think you are?

346
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:57,000
Is that mug of yours worth 140 grand?

347
00:16:57,680 --> 00:16:59,560
Go ahead, call them. Go on...

348
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:01,400
Call, get her locked up for ten years.

349
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:02,720
Go ahead.

350
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:07,280
See if a single cent lands in your pocket then.

351
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:08,480
Think it over.

352
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:15,319
Everything's open to discussion, right?

353
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:17,240
I charged you 1,800 in total,

354
00:17:17,319 --> 00:17:18,960
and bam, you demand 150 grand.

355
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:21,079
I'd love to give you 200 million—if I had it.

356
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:22,240
Is any of this realistic?

357
00:17:22,319 --> 00:17:23,160
How about this:

358
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:25,280
You refund her the 1,800,

359
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:27,319
and we pay another 30 grand on top. Deal?

360
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:28,280
What am I, a dog you're shooing off?

361
00:17:28,359 --> 00:17:29,640
You think I'm some beggar?

362
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:31,200
Give me the phone. I'm calling the cops.

363
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:34,600
Then how much do you want?

364
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:38,800
100 grand.

365
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:41,680
-I can't come up with 100 grand.
-Haggle any more and this talk's over.

366
00:17:42,240 --> 00:17:43,400
100 grand, flat.

367
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:45,160
Signed and sealed.

368
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:47,240
Set in stone. No backing out.

369
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:54,320
Careful...

370
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:57,640
Take care now.

371
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,560
Sorry about all this, Xu-jie.

372
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:01,640
Take care, Xu-jie.

373
00:18:02,760 --> 00:18:04,600
Who are you "Xu-jie"-ing?

374
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:05,920
She looks older than me.

375
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:08,120
No money by end of week, we meet at the police station.

376
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,680
Got it, Xu-jie.

377
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:12,680
Watch your step. Hold on to me.

378
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:31,920
Liu-ge.

379
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,240
I'm looking to sell my taxi plate.

380
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:34,680
Can you ask around for me?

381
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:35,960
What's it going for now?

382
00:18:37,040 --> 00:18:38,120
It dropped again?

383
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,880
100 grand works too.

384
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:41,120
I need cash.

385
00:18:42,560 --> 00:18:43,720
I'll wait to hear from you.

386
00:18:54,560 --> 00:18:56,280
Shit, gave them too much corn.

387
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:15,800
What's wrong?

388
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:17,800
Why are you crying?

389
00:19:18,480 --> 00:19:19,880
I'm not blaming you.

390
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:22,840
Besides, isn't it all sorted now?

391
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:23,840
Stop crying, okay?

392
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:27,240
Where am I supposed to scrape up 100 grand?

393
00:19:27,320 --> 00:19:29,040
Not your problem. I've got a plan.

394
00:19:29,120 --> 00:19:30,480
It's no big deal.

395
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:32,840
You just had to stir things up.

396
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:35,080
Buying a car behind my back...

397
00:19:35,160 --> 00:19:38,240
If it weren't for you, I'd have my own shop by now.

398
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:40,640
Would any of this have happened?

399
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:48,280
Okay, that's enough crying.

400
00:19:48,360 --> 00:19:49,360
Don't touch me.

401
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:53,360
Money's gone, we'll earn more.

402
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,680
Once my racing pigeons hatch,

403
00:19:55,760 --> 00:19:57,800
I flip them, and we're sitting on a good 150 grand.

404
00:19:58,600 --> 00:20:00,640
Problems money can solve aren't real problems.

405
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:01,880
Is that even a problem?

406
00:20:07,160 --> 00:20:10,000
How did we let our lives end up like this?

407
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:13,920
Don't you worry.

408
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:16,760
Once my pigeons are nesting,

409
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:18,480
we'll be right back on our feet.

410
00:20:19,080 --> 00:20:20,640
We're in the capital accumulation phase.

411
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:23,560
Next step, we leap up a class.

412
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:25,080
Financial freedom.

413
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:26,600
You know what financial freedom is?

414
00:20:26,680 --> 00:20:29,200
Making money without lifting a finger. That's freedom.

415
00:20:29,280 --> 00:20:31,080
Money making money, you know?

416
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:37,400
I really envy you.

417
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:41,000
You get to live in a dream forever.

418
00:20:41,080 --> 00:20:42,600
What's so bad about that?

419
00:20:42,680 --> 00:20:45,160
Dreams are just a reflection of reality.

420
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:46,880
That's Freud, you know.

421
00:20:47,360 --> 00:20:48,560
Biaozi.

422
00:20:49,520 --> 00:20:50,880
Let's get divorced.

423
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:16,640
Xiaobei's room is sitting empty, right?

424
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:19,240
Xiaobei's room isn't ours to give out.

425
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:21,800
It's fine. Try it.

426
00:21:26,360 --> 00:21:27,800
I can't even stretch my legs.

427
00:21:27,880 --> 00:21:29,520
It's two meters long.

428
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:31,880
How about I take your room? We can squeeze in.

429
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:33,680
Forget it. I'm a light sleeper.

430
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:36,480
Your grinding, farting, lip-smacking full-service package—

431
00:21:36,560 --> 00:21:37,480
I can't take it.

432
00:21:37,560 --> 00:21:39,480
I'm still a guest here, aren't I?

433
00:21:39,560 --> 00:21:40,880
And we're family, on top of that.

434
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:43,560
I'm already wounded enough from Liru.

435
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:45,240
Can't you treat me a little better?

436
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:47,120
If you and Liru get divorced,

437
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,600
you and I are coworkers at best.

438
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:50,080
Where are you going?

439
00:21:50,560 --> 00:21:51,400
Kitchen.

440
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:55,800
Can I smoke in the bathroom, then?

441
00:21:56,920 --> 00:21:57,920
Fine.

442
00:21:59,040 --> 00:22:00,640
Can I at least get a pillow?

443
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:02,840
Wash your feet before bed.

444
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:04,040
That smell!

445
00:22:16,200 --> 00:22:17,280
What are you doing here?

446
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:19,160
What, not welcome?

447
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:22,200
I'll get you a towel.

448
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:28,000
-Biaozi.
-What?! I'm taking a shit!

449
00:22:28,880 --> 00:22:29,880
Never mind the towel.

450
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:32,480
I got word on Fu Weijun.

451
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:42,280
He died in prison last month.

452
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:46,200
Dead?

453
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:54,080
(Public Telephone)

454
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:58,120
(Public Telephone)

455
00:23:07,880 --> 00:23:11,040
Page 9532657 for me.

456
00:23:11,120 --> 00:23:16,240
Leave a message: "Jun-ge and I have arrived in Songhe."

457
00:23:38,640 --> 00:23:39,680
Boss.

458
00:23:43,080 --> 00:23:44,040
Boss.

459
00:23:45,080 --> 00:23:46,280
Lend me a couple tokens.

460
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:49,200
Who borrows these things?

461
00:23:49,280 --> 00:23:51,600
Got money, you play. No money, go home.

462
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:54,760
When my folks get back, I'll pay you back, okay?

463
00:23:54,840 --> 00:23:56,680
-Just this once.
-No can do.

464
00:23:56,760 --> 00:23:57,840
Now scram.

465
00:24:01,120 --> 00:24:02,320
50 yuan in tokens.

466
00:24:10,400 --> 00:24:11,520
What's up?

467
00:24:11,600 --> 00:24:12,480
Out of tokens?

468
00:24:17,880 --> 00:24:19,000
Here, take two.

469
00:24:19,640 --> 00:24:20,720
Thanks, bro.

470
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:25,640
What were you playing just now?

471
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:27,560
The King of Fighters.

472
00:24:29,800 --> 00:24:30,880
Any good at it?

473
00:24:31,400 --> 00:24:32,600
I'm okay.

474
00:24:33,960 --> 00:24:37,280
I don't like playing against the machine.

475
00:24:37,360 --> 00:24:39,400
How about a couple rounds with me?

476
00:24:40,200 --> 00:24:41,400
I, uh...

477
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:44,160
Win, and it costs you nothing.

478
00:24:44,240 --> 00:24:46,160
Lose, and you use my tokens.

479
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:47,400
Deal.

480
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:48,720
I'll drop the coin for you.

481
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:56,560
What's your name?

482
00:24:56,640 --> 00:24:57,640
Shen Hui.

483
00:25:14,640 --> 00:25:15,640
Bro.

484
00:25:17,560 --> 00:25:18,640
You're back?

485
00:25:19,680 --> 00:25:21,200
Let's play a couple more rounds.

486
00:25:21,280 --> 00:25:23,520
I'm done. My mom's waiting at home.

487
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:27,520
Who are you trying to fool?

488
00:25:28,200 --> 00:25:30,640
Don't you live at your grandma's?

489
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:37,080
Aren't your folks away on a trip?

490
00:25:39,240 --> 00:25:40,480
They're back?

491
00:25:43,880 --> 00:25:45,440
What, did they fly home?

492
00:25:46,920 --> 00:25:48,920
I... I really can't play anymore.

493
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:51,200
My grandma's gonna start worrying.

494
00:26:09,800 --> 00:26:14,000
How can you just turn your back on me?

495
00:26:16,360 --> 00:26:21,600
Is that all our friendship's worth?

496
00:26:24,120 --> 00:26:25,200
Fine.

497
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:31,040
Pay me back for all those tokens.

498
00:26:31,120 --> 00:26:33,240
I... I don't have any money.

499
00:26:33,960 --> 00:26:35,040
I...

500
00:26:35,840 --> 00:26:37,600
I... I'm broke.

501
00:26:39,440 --> 00:26:41,040
No money? Then what do we do?

502
00:26:45,360 --> 00:26:47,960
N... nothing in here either.

503
00:26:49,440 --> 00:26:52,160
-I... I really have nothing.
-We'll tell your teacher!

504
00:26:58,680 --> 00:26:59,720
Bro.

505
00:27:15,360 --> 00:27:17,640
My brother asked you something.

506
00:27:18,280 --> 00:27:21,320
It's fine if you've got no money.

507
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:24,880
What'll you trade for it?

508
00:27:30,680 --> 00:27:32,080
What'll you trade?

509
00:27:33,800 --> 00:27:35,360
Bro, what do you want?

510
00:27:38,640 --> 00:27:41,120
Bro, what do you want?

511
00:27:52,800 --> 00:27:54,600
Your hand.

512
00:27:57,400 --> 00:27:58,640
A foot works too.

513
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:07,440
Let me go... please, bro, I'm begging you...

514
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:09,480
Let me go, don't...

515
00:28:09,560 --> 00:28:10,400
Bro...

516
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:12,200
Bro, let me go, please, don't...

517
00:28:12,280 --> 00:28:14,160
No... let me go, bro.

518
00:28:14,240 --> 00:28:15,320
Don't...

519
00:28:15,400 --> 00:28:17,760
"Typically attached at both ends to two

520
00:28:17,840 --> 00:28:20,480
or more bones.

521
00:28:20,560 --> 00:28:23,800
One: master the anatomical arrangement of skeletal muscles

522
00:28:23,880 --> 00:28:26,040
and their accessory structures.

523
00:28:26,120 --> 00:28:27,720
Two: master the trapezius

524
00:28:27,800 --> 00:28:29,720
and the location and function of the latissimus dorsi.

525
00:28:29,800 --> 00:28:31,640
Three: master the pectoralis major

526
00:28:31,720 --> 00:28:34,000
and the location and function of the serratus anterior,

527
00:28:34,080 --> 00:28:35,800
the location, form, and function of the diaphragm,

528
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:39,240
and the names and locations of its three openings."

529
00:28:47,120 --> 00:28:48,440
What's wrong, ma'am?

530
00:28:50,160 --> 00:28:51,360
What happened?

531
00:28:52,120 --> 00:28:53,560
It's all my fault.

532
00:28:54,080 --> 00:28:55,880
Going so far away to see a doctor...

533
00:28:55,960 --> 00:28:57,920
Otherwise little Hui wouldn't have gotten hurt this bad.

534
00:28:58,000 --> 00:28:59,320
Stop that wailing.

535
00:29:03,480 --> 00:29:04,600
I'll go check out.

536
00:29:40,120 --> 00:29:41,520
Don't let it eat you up too much.

537
00:29:42,040 --> 00:29:43,320
A broken arm is just an external injury.

538
00:29:43,400 --> 00:29:44,440
It heals up fine.

539
00:29:49,040 --> 00:29:50,120
What did you say?

540
00:29:51,880 --> 00:29:54,920
But next time, it might not just be an arm.

541
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:56,640
Go home with your auntie and heal up.

542
00:29:56,720 --> 00:29:58,160
And don't come back.

543
00:30:06,840 --> 00:30:10,000
You will die by my hand, sooner or later.

544
00:30:10,560 --> 00:30:12,040
I mean it.

545
00:30:27,600 --> 00:30:28,800
Sooner or later,

546
00:30:30,880 --> 00:30:32,360
you'll die by my hand.

547
00:31:43,440 --> 00:31:45,560
Yang'er, dinner's ready.

548
00:31:45,640 --> 00:31:46,920
I'm not eating, Ma.

549
00:31:54,280 --> 00:31:55,240
What's wrong, Ma?

550
00:31:55,320 --> 00:31:56,280
You okay?

551
00:31:57,280 --> 00:31:58,720
I feel a bit sick.

552
00:32:01,160 --> 00:32:02,120
What's wrong?

553
00:32:02,200 --> 00:32:03,200
It's just a passing spell.

554
00:32:05,720 --> 00:32:07,480
Sit down and eat something, it'll pass.

555
00:32:08,600 --> 00:32:10,440
It's just the cooking fumes.

556
00:32:11,160 --> 00:32:12,560
Eat something and you'll be fine.

557
00:32:12,640 --> 00:32:15,000
Come on, you... sit and keep me company, eat a little.

558
00:32:15,080 --> 00:32:16,080
Come on.

559
00:32:18,040 --> 00:32:19,640
All your favorites.

560
00:32:30,080 --> 00:32:31,760
Still mad at your dad?

561
00:32:39,280 --> 00:32:41,360
Your dad means well too.

562
00:32:41,440 --> 00:32:44,800
He's just scared Xing San'er won't let it go and it'll ruin your factory placement.

563
00:32:44,880 --> 00:32:46,720
After hitting you, no one hurt more than him.

564
00:32:46,800 --> 00:32:47,680
He regrets it to death.

565
00:32:48,240 --> 00:32:49,480
He didn't sleep a wink last night.

566
00:32:49,560 --> 00:32:51,720
Woke up with two big blisters on his lip.

567
00:32:53,560 --> 00:32:55,080
How could I not be mad?

568
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:58,160
On the street, in front of all those people, he just hit me.

569
00:32:58,240 --> 00:33:00,640
Besides, is getting into the factory really that important?

570
00:33:00,720 --> 00:33:01,800
Right.

571
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:04,400
Only factory work counts as a real job?

572
00:33:04,480 --> 00:33:06,160
And what I do isn't a real job?

573
00:33:06,720 --> 00:33:10,160
It's all labor. How does he get to rank it high and low?

574
00:33:12,880 --> 00:33:14,080
Look,

575
00:33:14,840 --> 00:33:16,640
you really should try to understand your dad.

576
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:18,080
Our generation,

577
00:33:18,160 --> 00:33:20,080
we got used to having our lives arranged for us.

578
00:33:20,800 --> 00:33:23,040
As kids, with so many children at home,

579
00:33:23,120 --> 00:33:24,720
you obeyed your parents in everything.

580
00:33:24,800 --> 00:33:26,400
Grown up, out in the collective,

581
00:33:26,480 --> 00:33:28,200
of course you obeyed your leaders.

582
00:33:28,280 --> 00:33:31,400
People like us, our whole lives, we felt like...

583
00:33:31,480 --> 00:33:32,680
that around us,

584
00:33:33,160 --> 00:33:34,960
there was a circle.

585
00:33:35,040 --> 00:33:36,360
We stayed right there,

586
00:33:36,440 --> 00:33:39,080
plodding along inside that circle, step by step.

587
00:33:39,160 --> 00:33:40,560
Nobody asked why.

588
00:33:40,640 --> 00:33:42,680
Nobody ever wandered outside it.

589
00:33:42,760 --> 00:33:45,240
Even stepping on the line was scary.

590
00:33:48,920 --> 00:33:51,200
The world's changing so fast now.

591
00:33:51,280 --> 00:33:53,400
Every generation has its own way of living.

592
00:33:54,160 --> 00:33:55,640
Someday, when you have kids,

593
00:33:56,160 --> 00:33:57,880
you might not figure them out either.

594
00:33:58,560 --> 00:33:59,560
But understood or not,

595
00:33:59,640 --> 00:34:01,720
a father and son are always father and son.

596
00:34:02,720 --> 00:34:04,840
Don't hold a grudge against your dad. Hear me?

597
00:34:06,320 --> 00:34:07,760
I don't hold grudges against him.

598
00:34:07,840 --> 00:34:09,639
I'm not petty like him.

599
00:34:09,719 --> 00:34:10,679
That's good.

600
00:34:11,199 --> 00:34:12,800
Come on, eat. Hurry up.

601
00:34:12,880 --> 00:34:14,040
Eat something.

602
00:34:15,520 --> 00:34:16,520
Here.

603
00:34:18,960 --> 00:34:19,880
Ma.

604
00:34:21,360 --> 00:34:22,600
I need to go out for a bit.

605
00:34:24,840 --> 00:34:26,239
Eat something before you go

606
00:34:26,320 --> 00:34:27,360
I'm good

607
00:34:31,679 --> 00:34:33,719
Alright, go on then. Back early.

608
00:34:35,199 --> 00:34:36,440
I'm off, Ma

609
00:34:37,760 --> 00:34:39,000
Bye, Ma

610
00:34:52,800 --> 00:34:54,639
Hey—don't go any further in

611
00:34:54,719 --> 00:34:56,040
No late show today

612
00:34:56,120 --> 00:34:57,480
I'm here for Shen Mo

613
00:34:58,040 --> 00:34:59,240
We made plans

614
00:35:07,880 --> 00:35:08,880
You're here this early?

615
00:35:14,320 --> 00:35:15,840
"Titanic"?

616
00:35:15,920 --> 00:35:17,160
We couldn't watch it together last time

617
00:35:17,240 --> 00:35:18,920
Here's your chance to make up for it

618
00:35:23,920 --> 00:35:25,480
This is Wang Yang

619
00:35:27,160 --> 00:35:28,440
This is Fu Weijun

620
00:35:29,200 --> 00:35:31,080
I'll go see if I can get it playing

621
00:35:49,600 --> 00:35:52,840
Hey buddy, you just met Shen Mo, right?

622
00:35:52,920 --> 00:35:54,160
Never heard her mention you either

623
00:35:57,280 --> 00:35:58,640
Hey, I'm talking to you

624
00:36:00,280 --> 00:36:01,440
He can't hear you

625
00:36:02,240 --> 00:36:03,520
You could've said so

626
00:36:03,600 --> 00:36:05,080
Almost swung at him

627
00:36:26,200 --> 00:36:27,240
The hell's he mean?

628
00:36:27,320 --> 00:36:28,960
My brother says you're a bit slow

629
00:37:13,880 --> 00:37:15,120
Your surname's Shen

630
00:37:15,200 --> 00:37:16,920
So why's your brother a Fu?

631
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:20,480
My brother's a year younger

632
00:37:20,560 --> 00:37:21,800
After my parents died,

633
00:37:21,880 --> 00:37:23,680
we went to live with my uncle

634
00:37:23,760 --> 00:37:27,680
My aunt didn't want him—his ears were bad

635
00:37:28,200 --> 00:37:30,600
So they gave him to a family in Hualin

636
00:37:30,680 --> 00:37:32,120
That family named him

637
00:37:32,200 --> 00:37:33,600
He got used to it

638
00:37:34,600 --> 00:37:36,320
Then that family had a kid of their own

639
00:37:36,400 --> 00:37:38,120
so he went to the orphanage

640
00:37:38,720 --> 00:37:41,400
I tested into Hualin Med just to see him

641
00:37:43,240 --> 00:37:45,000
He's the only family I've got left

642
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:49,960
Isn't there one more now?

643
00:38:39,600 --> 00:38:40,640
Cui Guodong

644
00:38:43,240 --> 00:38:44,400
Down here

645
00:38:46,640 --> 00:38:47,840
Who found it?

646
00:38:47,920 --> 00:38:49,160
The patrol team

647
00:38:49,680 --> 00:38:51,600
- Right in this drainage ditch
- Let me

648
00:38:51,680 --> 00:38:52,760
Easy there

649
00:38:53,320 --> 00:38:54,520
Move, let me see

650
00:38:55,440 --> 00:38:56,800
Step aside

651
00:38:56,880 --> 00:38:59,600
Didn't you mark some underground drain points?

652
00:39:00,080 --> 00:39:02,320
Had the patrol team sweep them for us

653
00:39:03,080 --> 00:39:04,560
They just got to this spot

654
00:39:05,400 --> 00:39:06,920
That Wang Xiang, huh

655
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:21,680
What is it?

656
00:39:24,080 --> 00:39:26,080
This killer's a fucking monster

657
00:39:34,280 --> 00:39:36,080
Found a backpack in the pipe too

658
00:39:36,600 --> 00:39:38,440
Inside's a meal card from Hualin Med

659
00:39:43,760 --> 00:39:45,640
Leave the feelings out. Work.

660
00:39:48,240 --> 00:39:49,160
Move along...

661
00:39:49,680 --> 00:39:50,720
Stop looking

662
00:39:54,040 --> 00:39:55,280
Search it real careful

663
00:40:29,680 --> 00:40:32,000
Reading this junk all day—how'll you get into college?

664
00:40:35,320 --> 00:40:37,080
("The Death of Ah Lu")

665
00:40:40,120 --> 00:40:41,480
"At a moment like this

666
00:40:41,560 --> 00:40:44,040
let me die before my father

667
00:40:44,560 --> 00:40:47,120
let my mother, with her final elegy,

668
00:40:47,200 --> 00:40:51,120
keep vigil for me, and for the earth's four seasons"

669
00:40:52,880 --> 00:40:54,360
What kinda crap poem is this?

670
00:40:54,440 --> 00:40:55,840
No meter, no rhyme

671
00:41:00,160 --> 00:41:01,320
Where'd it go?

672
00:41:17,720 --> 00:41:18,680
Good Lord

673
00:41:19,240 --> 00:41:21,200
This room looks like it got robbed

674
00:41:21,720 --> 00:41:22,800
Dad

675
00:41:22,880 --> 00:41:24,560
What's this thing doing here?

676
00:41:24,640 --> 00:41:26,520
I haven't used it in years

677
00:41:28,520 --> 00:41:30,800
Wore it hiking with Qu Bo a couple days back

678
00:41:31,360 --> 00:41:32,280
This thing beats the cold

679
00:41:32,360 --> 00:41:33,400
Hiking what?

680
00:41:33,960 --> 00:41:35,120
A snow mountain?

681
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:38,280
Where's our old map gone?

682
00:41:38,360 --> 00:41:40,000
I remember sticking it in a cookbook

683
00:41:40,680 --> 00:41:41,800
It's up here

684
00:41:43,960 --> 00:41:45,800
What's it doing up there?

685
00:41:48,920 --> 00:41:49,880
No—

686
00:41:49,960 --> 00:41:51,680
What do you want the map for?

687
00:41:51,760 --> 00:41:52,840
The dismemberment case

688
00:41:52,920 --> 00:41:55,160
Helping the police canvass the plant

689
00:41:55,240 --> 00:41:57,080
I'm briefing Xing San'er and his bunch

690
00:41:57,160 --> 00:41:58,680
Wait, you're skipping lunch?

691
00:41:58,760 --> 00:42:01,200
This matters more than lunch

692
00:42:01,840 --> 00:42:03,560
You never stop, do you?

693
00:42:14,480 --> 00:42:15,560
Master Wang

694
00:42:16,080 --> 00:42:18,440
That train sits any longer, it'll rust shut

695
00:42:19,400 --> 00:42:20,520
Relax

696
00:42:21,360 --> 00:42:23,960
With me around, not even a lug nut rusts

697
00:42:24,040 --> 00:42:25,400
It'll outlive you

698
00:42:30,240 --> 00:42:31,640
Isn't that Security's kettle?

699
00:42:31,720 --> 00:42:32,960
New post, Master Wang?

700
00:42:33,840 --> 00:42:35,680
Been given other duties lately

701
00:42:35,760 --> 00:42:37,120
Giving Security some training

702
00:42:37,680 --> 00:42:38,680
You? Training them?

703
00:42:39,400 --> 00:42:41,560
Gotta lecture your workshop sometime too

704
00:42:42,120 --> 00:42:43,600
The title:

705
00:42:43,680 --> 00:42:46,640
"Stay Alert, Keep Your Eyes Peeled"

706
00:43:12,600 --> 00:43:14,240
No manners at all

707
00:43:17,920 --> 00:43:19,080
Master Wang

708
00:43:19,960 --> 00:43:20,920
Don't go

709
00:43:21,000 --> 00:43:22,560
The meeting hasn't started

710
00:43:22,640 --> 00:43:23,800
Where is everyone?

711
00:43:24,520 --> 00:43:26,400
Meeting's at one. Where's Security?

712
00:43:28,360 --> 00:43:29,240
Master Wang

713
00:43:29,320 --> 00:43:30,960
Thing is, Captain Ma just called me

714
00:43:31,520 --> 00:43:33,920
Says the plant sweep's gotta be us two teamed up

715
00:43:34,000 --> 00:43:35,360
The moment I heard that,

716
00:43:35,960 --> 00:43:37,120
I felt solid

717
00:43:37,200 --> 00:43:38,720
Cut the crap

718
00:43:38,800 --> 00:43:40,400
About our internal sweep,

719
00:43:40,480 --> 00:43:41,800
here's my thinking

720
00:43:41,880 --> 00:43:42,920
Master Wang,

721
00:43:43,600 --> 00:43:45,320
here's where things stand

722
00:43:47,800 --> 00:43:50,640
We've picked up a bit of his trail

723
00:43:53,800 --> 00:43:54,640
Who?

724
00:43:54,720 --> 00:43:56,240
Don't know who he is yet

725
00:43:56,320 --> 00:43:59,280
But looks like the killer did show his face in our plant

726
00:44:05,040 --> 00:44:06,720
Why's Security empty?

727
00:44:14,560 --> 00:44:16,200
All out manning the net

728
00:44:16,960 --> 00:44:17,800
The net?

729
00:44:17,880 --> 00:44:18,800
That's right

730
00:44:24,680 --> 00:44:26,920
Well? Find anything?

731
00:44:27,000 --> 00:44:28,200
Nothing

732
00:44:28,280 --> 00:44:29,400
Dazhi,

733
00:44:29,480 --> 00:44:31,000
tell Master Wang

734
00:44:31,080 --> 00:44:32,600
everything you saw that night

735
00:44:34,440 --> 00:44:36,200
So, that night,

736
00:44:36,280 --> 00:44:37,440
I'd just come off shift

737
00:44:38,360 --> 00:44:40,600
Carrying my stuff, figuring I'd hit the baths

738
00:44:40,680 --> 00:44:43,760
I'm walking along by the furnaces, walking...

739
00:44:44,320 --> 00:44:45,560
walking...

740
00:44:46,040 --> 00:44:47,400
when all of a sudden

741
00:44:48,040 --> 00:44:49,920
I hear a noise

742
00:44:52,040 --> 00:44:52,960
What noise?

743
00:44:53,040 --> 00:44:56,200
When I stop, it stops

744
00:44:56,680 --> 00:44:58,360
When I walk, it walks too

745
00:44:59,760 --> 00:45:02,320
So I look up along the furnace

746
00:45:03,280 --> 00:45:04,360
And?

747
00:45:04,440 --> 00:45:06,240
There's a guy in a protective suit

748
00:45:06,320 --> 00:45:07,520
standing on top of the furnace

749
00:45:08,480 --> 00:45:09,560
He turns around—

750
00:45:10,400 --> 00:45:11,720
the face is blank

751
00:45:13,920 --> 00:45:15,400
Blank face?

752
00:45:16,440 --> 00:45:17,320
Bullshit

753
00:45:17,400 --> 00:45:20,080
If I'm lying, I'm a bastard

754
00:45:20,920 --> 00:45:22,800
Wait—you couldn't see his face at all

755
00:45:22,880 --> 00:45:24,760
So how do you figure he's the killer?

756
00:45:24,840 --> 00:45:27,080
- Well, it's...
- Yeah, based on what?

757
00:45:27,160 --> 00:45:28,240
Think about it

758
00:45:28,320 --> 00:45:30,800
A guy who cuts a person into slices—

759
00:45:30,880 --> 00:45:32,040
you telling me he ain't evil?

760
00:45:32,120 --> 00:45:34,120
There's a killing aura on his head

761
00:45:34,200 --> 00:45:35,520
Dazhi saw it. Did you?

762
00:45:36,200 --> 00:45:37,240
See?

763
00:45:40,000 --> 00:45:43,120
Can't see his face, but you saw an aura?

764
00:45:43,640 --> 00:45:45,800
This is pointless. You two, beat it.

765
00:45:47,160 --> 00:45:49,160
Wang Xiang, listen to me

766
00:45:49,680 --> 00:45:51,200
He came once

767
00:45:51,280 --> 00:45:53,320
No guarantee he won't come twice

768
00:45:54,120 --> 00:45:56,320
I've thrown all of Security out there

769
00:45:56,840 --> 00:45:57,960
Every plant gate,

770
00:45:58,040 --> 00:45:59,400
every main road—

771
00:45:59,480 --> 00:46:01,200
if it can be covered, I've covered it

772
00:46:01,280 --> 00:46:03,320
Male, under 180 cm,

773
00:46:03,400 --> 00:46:05,160
killing aura on his head

774
00:46:05,240 --> 00:46:07,360
Under 180 cm, male,

775
00:46:07,440 --> 00:46:08,760
aura on the head

776
00:46:08,840 --> 00:46:11,320
This plant's got 800 of those, easy

777
00:46:11,400 --> 00:46:13,680
People can barely eat—who ain't got an aura?

778
00:46:16,520 --> 00:46:19,520
Wang Xiang, you're an old-timer of this plant

779
00:46:19,600 --> 00:46:21,240
Show a little awareness

780
00:46:21,320 --> 00:46:25,160
The smelting shop is the prime spot he was seen

781
00:46:25,240 --> 00:46:27,080
I'm saving it for you

782
00:46:28,160 --> 00:46:30,000
Why not report straight to Captain Ma?

783
00:46:30,080 --> 00:46:31,720
It's just your word, no proof

784
00:46:31,800 --> 00:46:33,360
So? You staking this spot or not?

785
00:46:33,440 --> 00:46:35,000
- You won't, I hand it to someone else
- What?

786
00:46:35,080 --> 00:46:37,160
Who says I won't? Course I'll stake it!

787
00:46:40,840 --> 00:46:44,400
But what would the killer want at the smelting shop?

788
00:46:44,480 --> 00:46:46,920
Catch him and ask him yourself

789
00:46:48,720 --> 00:46:50,520
- What's this?
- What? A whistle.

790
00:46:50,600 --> 00:46:51,720
What for?

791
00:46:51,800 --> 00:46:53,640
Blow it the second you spot something

792
00:46:53,720 --> 00:46:55,240
Backup swarms in from all directions

793
00:46:55,320 --> 00:46:56,200
Here

794
00:46:56,680 --> 00:46:57,840
You take a two-hour watch

795
00:46:57,920 --> 00:46:58,840
I'll come relieve you

796
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:40,880
You?

797
00:47:43,840 --> 00:47:44,720
You?

798
00:47:49,360 --> 00:47:51,040
Ten to ace, pair of sevens

799
00:47:51,120 --> 00:47:52,360
Lemme see your hand

800
00:47:52,440 --> 00:47:54,120
- Damn
- You're short a pair of twos

801
00:47:54,200 --> 00:47:56,120
You play like absolute garbage

802
00:47:56,200 --> 00:47:57,960
- Again... deal
- Come on... Chief Xing

803
00:48:00,720 --> 00:48:02,480
There's still a guy in the smelting shop

804
00:48:03,120 --> 00:48:04,840
What? You wanna cover his shift?

805
00:48:04,920 --> 00:48:06,160
Not a chance

806
00:48:06,760 --> 00:48:08,400
He dreams of earning glory, don't he?

807
00:48:08,480 --> 00:48:09,520
Let him snap out of it

808
00:48:10,080 --> 00:48:12,840
A lousy driver reaching into my Security Section

809
00:48:13,560 --> 00:48:14,840
City Bureau? So what?

810
00:48:15,560 --> 00:48:17,280
Detective captain? So what?

811
00:48:17,360 --> 00:48:18,600
I'm fucking laying it down here:

812
00:48:18,680 --> 00:48:21,080
inside Hualin Steel, none of it flies

813
00:48:21,160 --> 00:48:22,920
- Third Brother's the man...
- Exactly

814
00:48:23,000 --> 00:48:24,000
Damn right

815
00:48:24,760 --> 00:48:25,760
Chief Xing

816
00:48:27,000 --> 00:48:29,840
But what if Dazhi really saw the killer?

817
00:48:29,920 --> 00:48:31,880
Would a real killer get caught by him?

818
00:48:32,800 --> 00:48:34,240
He's playing a cute little game

819
00:48:34,840 --> 00:48:36,440
thinks this'll be his big comeback

820
00:48:39,440 --> 00:48:40,520
Liru

821
00:48:41,480 --> 00:48:42,560
Liru

822
00:48:44,000 --> 00:48:44,840
Here

823
00:48:47,720 --> 00:48:49,160
What took you so long?

824
00:48:49,240 --> 00:48:50,920
I rushed over from your hospital

825
00:48:51,000 --> 00:48:53,360
My hospital? We said we'd meet here.

826
00:48:53,440 --> 00:48:55,480
Something came up at the plant office

827
00:48:56,080 --> 00:48:59,040
Old Zhao—Director Zhao—got jumped by two workers in the canteen

828
00:48:59,600 --> 00:49:01,080
Blood spraying everywhere

829
00:49:01,160 --> 00:49:02,800
I was out the door and they called me back

830
00:49:02,880 --> 00:49:04,760
Those office guys can't handle shit

831
00:49:05,240 --> 00:49:07,280
I don't go back, it all falls apart

832
00:49:08,680 --> 00:49:11,120
I'm off work. Spare me the plant talk.

833
00:49:12,000 --> 00:49:14,000
Sorry—kept you waiting till you starved

834
00:49:14,760 --> 00:49:15,800
You only bought one?

835
00:49:15,880 --> 00:49:17,160
We watching the movie or not?

836
00:49:18,120 --> 00:49:20,120
We are. I picked it special.

837
00:49:20,680 --> 00:49:22,560
A love story. Real romantic.

838
00:49:22,640 --> 00:49:24,800
Hang on, let me park my bike

839
00:49:30,120 --> 00:49:31,280
Where'd you get that roast sweet potato?

840
00:49:31,360 --> 00:49:32,680
Get me one too

841
00:49:49,440 --> 00:49:50,920
Some pick...

842
00:49:51,000 --> 00:49:53,720
Never knew romance could be like this

843
00:49:54,560 --> 00:49:57,960
From the title, I figured Yu Dafu, Lin Huiyin, that stuff

844
00:49:59,160 --> 00:50:00,800
It's pretty romantic, actually

845
00:50:02,040 --> 00:50:04,440
Just a bit shaky. Making me dizzy.

846
00:50:06,680 --> 00:50:09,560
That actor kinda looks like you

847
00:50:10,480 --> 00:50:11,440
Oh yeah?

848
00:50:13,400 --> 00:50:15,600
People used to say I belonged in the movies

849
00:50:16,760 --> 00:50:19,200
Then I went all-in on academics. Missed the boat.

850
00:50:24,400 --> 00:50:27,200
Did your brother-in-law tell you my basics?

851
00:50:28,680 --> 00:50:29,760
Who?

852
00:50:31,000 --> 00:50:32,240
Master Wang

853
00:50:36,920 --> 00:50:38,800
He... didn't really say much

854
00:50:44,400 --> 00:50:45,880
Well, here's the deal

855
00:50:46,480 --> 00:50:49,840
Career first, then family, right?

856
00:50:51,080 --> 00:50:55,440
I'm right in the rising phase of my career

857
00:50:56,080 --> 00:50:58,920
Plant office, after Director Zhao, it's me

858
00:51:07,640 --> 00:51:09,640
Speak normally. I can hear you.

859
00:51:12,480 --> 00:51:14,320
Freud said it:

860
00:51:15,120 --> 00:51:18,440
"A mentally healthy person can do two things:

861
00:51:19,200 --> 00:51:20,520
work with devotion

862
00:51:20,600 --> 00:51:21,920
and love"

863
00:51:22,840 --> 00:51:24,040
On the work front,

864
00:51:24,120 --> 00:51:26,640
I've basically left everyone in the dust

865
00:51:27,440 --> 00:51:29,760
All that's left is love

866
00:51:30,560 --> 00:51:32,000
Who's Freud?

867
00:51:32,880 --> 00:51:34,360
A scholar

868
00:51:34,440 --> 00:51:36,280
Studies dreams, mostly

869
00:51:36,360 --> 00:51:37,560
He get an apartment?

870
00:51:38,600 --> 00:51:40,920
Nope. He's not with our plant.

871
00:51:41,640 --> 00:51:42,760
Did you get one?

872
00:51:43,280 --> 00:51:44,360
Any day now

873
00:51:46,080 --> 00:51:49,600
Old Zhao and I have explored the matter in depth

874
00:51:50,800 --> 00:51:52,120
You see,

875
00:51:52,200 --> 00:51:54,560
Director Song values talent

876
00:51:54,640 --> 00:51:56,320
With my work ability,

877
00:51:56,400 --> 00:51:58,520
the next round's no problem

878
00:52:06,800 --> 00:52:07,800
Liru

879
00:52:08,360 --> 00:52:10,720
So, on the dating front,

880
00:52:10,800 --> 00:52:12,240
what's your type?

881
00:52:16,400 --> 00:52:18,360
I like the mature type

882
00:52:18,440 --> 00:52:20,080
Then I've got a huge edge

883
00:52:23,320 --> 00:52:24,840
What edge?

884
00:52:24,920 --> 00:52:27,440
People say I look a bit old for my age

885
00:52:34,600 --> 00:52:36,560
Watch the movie. Stop squirming.

886
00:52:36,640 --> 00:52:37,840
Your hair

887
00:52:41,800 --> 00:52:43,240
What's so good about it?

888
00:52:43,320 --> 00:52:45,840
Two grown men rolling around up there

889
00:52:51,000 --> 00:52:52,200
Liru

890
00:52:52,280 --> 00:52:54,080
Wait up—I'll see you home

891
00:53:01,080 --> 00:53:02,360
Hop on

892
00:53:02,440 --> 00:53:03,800
Aren't you heading back to the workers' dorm?

893
00:53:03,880 --> 00:53:05,080
It's not on your way

894
00:53:05,640 --> 00:53:06,960
Isn't the earth round?

895
00:53:07,040 --> 00:53:09,240
Off-route or not, a few extra steps gets me there

896
00:53:10,080 --> 00:53:11,440
Really, no need. Thanks.

897
00:53:12,120 --> 00:53:14,000
Let's pick another movie sometime

898
00:53:14,480 --> 00:53:16,320
We'll see. I'm off.

899
00:53:25,120 --> 00:53:27,000
Who pulled my valve core?

900
00:53:28,160 --> 00:53:29,960
Sweet potato man—did you see who?

901
00:54:20,120 --> 00:54:21,200
Master Wang

902
00:54:30,960 --> 00:54:32,360
Master Wang, you hungry?

903
00:54:32,960 --> 00:54:35,640
Let's go find a spot to eat

904
00:54:38,000 --> 00:54:39,280
Stand up first

905
00:54:40,360 --> 00:54:41,400
What's wrong?

906
00:54:45,920 --> 00:54:46,800
Turn around

907
00:54:51,600 --> 00:54:52,640
What are you doing?

908
00:54:52,720 --> 00:54:53,560
How tall?

909
00:54:53,640 --> 00:54:54,720
180 centimeters.

910
00:54:55,440 --> 00:54:56,640
Really?

911
00:54:56,720 --> 00:54:58,440
178.5 barefoot.

912
00:54:58,520 --> 00:54:59,680
180 in heels.

913
00:55:01,080 --> 00:55:02,680
I mean, you...

914
00:55:03,760 --> 00:55:05,560
You're a factory office guy.

915
00:55:06,400 --> 00:55:08,480
Why wear smelter overalls?

916
00:55:08,560 --> 00:55:09,960
Isn't that a safety hazard?

917
00:55:10,440 --> 00:55:12,440
Don't you need work clothes in the smelter?

918
00:55:13,360 --> 00:55:14,720
You play it real safe.

919
00:55:15,480 --> 00:55:16,560
Sit down.

920
00:55:25,720 --> 00:55:27,120
How did you know I was here?

921
00:55:27,200 --> 00:55:29,080
I went to the locomotive depot for you.

922
00:55:29,160 --> 00:55:30,920
They said you were at a Security Section meeting.

923
00:55:31,000 --> 00:55:32,680
So I went to Security for you.

924
00:55:32,760 --> 00:55:34,520
They told me to check the overhead crane.

925
00:55:34,600 --> 00:55:36,920
And I actually dug you out here.

926
00:55:38,360 --> 00:55:39,240
Is that how you talk?

927
00:55:40,440 --> 00:55:42,240
Who says "dug out" about finding someone?

928
00:55:42,320 --> 00:55:43,560
That's not what I meant.

929
00:55:45,840 --> 00:55:47,320
-This is "digging out."
-Yeah.

930
00:55:50,160 --> 00:55:52,280
Besides, I revealed myself on purpose.

931
00:55:52,360 --> 00:55:53,640
Otherwise, could you have found me?

932
00:55:53,720 --> 00:55:54,880
Right...

933
00:55:54,960 --> 00:55:56,320
You were so well hidden.

934
00:55:56,400 --> 00:55:58,400
I... I just misspoke.

935
00:56:02,320 --> 00:56:04,080
Stop eating that lousy potato.

936
00:56:04,760 --> 00:56:07,000
Let's go find a place to eat and talk.

937
00:56:07,080 --> 00:56:08,200
My treat.

938
00:56:09,480 --> 00:56:10,680
No merit, no reward.

939
00:56:12,280 --> 00:56:13,640
Why are you treating me?

940
00:56:16,960 --> 00:56:18,600
It's about me and Liru.

941
00:56:19,360 --> 00:56:21,040
Put in another push for me.

942
00:56:21,120 --> 00:56:22,440
You need my push?

943
00:56:23,040 --> 00:56:24,760
Didn't you take her to a movie?

944
00:56:25,320 --> 00:56:26,400
Don't bring it up.

945
00:56:27,400 --> 00:56:29,920
The movie choice was a bit of a mistake.

946
00:56:30,000 --> 00:56:31,360
Was that the movie's fault?

947
00:56:34,480 --> 00:56:35,960
No, Master Wang.

948
00:56:36,040 --> 00:56:37,280
Would I let you help for nothing?

949
00:56:43,120 --> 00:56:44,760
Where'd this liquor come from?

950
00:56:44,840 --> 00:56:46,000
Old Song gave it to me.

951
00:56:51,280 --> 00:56:54,760
Song Yukun gave you liquor?

952
00:56:54,840 --> 00:56:57,680
I got my classmate to tutor his son in English.

953
00:56:57,760 --> 00:56:58,640
Didn't take money.

954
00:56:58,720 --> 00:57:00,120
So he gave me this.

955
00:57:00,200 --> 00:57:01,800
Said this liquor's got age.

956
00:57:02,560 --> 00:57:04,640
By age, it'd be your elder.

957
00:57:05,200 --> 00:57:07,560
As long as you fix things with Liru and me,

958
00:57:07,640 --> 00:57:09,000
I'd call it Grandpa.

959
00:57:09,080 --> 00:57:09,920
Seriously.

960
00:57:10,000 --> 00:57:11,680
Is the factory office busy these days?

961
00:57:12,360 --> 00:57:13,440
Why?

962
00:57:14,480 --> 00:57:17,840
If not—I'm canvassing the factory now, right?

963
00:57:17,920 --> 00:57:19,200
Lend me a hand.

964
00:57:19,840 --> 00:57:21,760
Sure, no problem.

965
00:57:22,360 --> 00:57:23,920
Point, and I'll strike.

966
00:57:25,320 --> 00:57:26,640
Then about me and Liru...

967
00:57:28,120 --> 00:57:29,200
Just wait for word.

968
00:57:30,960 --> 00:57:32,160
Is it done?

969
00:57:33,000 --> 00:57:34,320
Break off a piece for me to taste.

970
00:57:40,040 --> 00:57:41,240
So good.

971
00:58:23,520 --> 00:58:24,400
Captain Ma.

972
00:58:24,880 --> 00:58:26,720
This is Shen Mo's counselor.

973
00:58:27,240 --> 00:58:29,000
-Ma Desheng, Criminal Police.
-Hello.

974
00:58:29,080 --> 00:58:30,200
Well?

975
00:58:30,280 --> 00:58:31,760
Is it Shen Mo's?

976
00:58:33,160 --> 00:58:34,960
Well... let's sit and talk.

977
00:58:35,880 --> 00:58:38,360
Shen Mo tested in from Songhe.

978
00:58:39,000 --> 00:58:40,960
She never talked much.

979
00:58:41,520 --> 00:58:42,840
A quiet girl.

980
00:58:43,440 --> 00:58:45,880
Grades above average, I'd say.

981
00:58:45,960 --> 00:58:47,880
Never gave us much worry.

982
00:58:47,960 --> 00:58:49,840
But a while back,

983
00:58:50,480 --> 00:58:52,360
something unusual came up.

984
00:58:55,160 --> 00:58:56,360
What situation?

985
00:59:01,960 --> 00:59:03,280
What? You can't say?

986
00:59:30,160 --> 00:59:31,120
Where'd these come from?

987
00:59:31,800 --> 00:59:33,200
Early on the 20th,

988
00:59:33,280 --> 00:59:35,560
these photos and the report letter

989
00:59:35,640 --> 00:59:39,560
were posted on the school cafeteria bulletin board.

990
00:59:39,640 --> 00:59:41,560
The letter also said

991
00:59:42,360 --> 00:59:47,840
Shen Mo worked as a call girl in a sex venue.

992
00:59:47,920 --> 00:59:49,480
Drinking and sleeping with clients.

993
00:59:49,560 --> 00:59:51,320
Why wasn't it reported?

994
00:59:52,920 --> 00:59:57,080
School leaders feared it would hurt the school's name.

995
01:00:04,880 --> 01:00:07,560
Some students also told me before

996
01:00:07,640 --> 01:00:09,880
her off-campus ties were complicated too.

997
01:00:09,960 --> 01:00:12,760
A boy kept coming to school for her.

998
01:00:12,840 --> 01:00:15,920
Right... that kid even wrote a self-criticism at our office.

999
01:00:46,400 --> 01:00:48,360
Master Wang, let's call it a day.

1000
01:00:49,240 --> 01:00:51,360
The office might look for me—I should head back.

1001
01:00:56,320 --> 01:00:58,280
What the hell? That's filthy.

1002
01:01:01,560 --> 01:01:03,640
Easy—this is quality fabric.

1003
01:01:07,840 --> 01:01:09,040
Shine it further in.

1004
01:01:09,880 --> 01:01:10,760
Shine it further in.

1005
01:01:10,840 --> 01:01:12,000
Further in.

1006
01:01:12,080 --> 01:01:13,000
That's the limit.

1007
01:01:13,680 --> 01:01:14,920
This one...

1008
01:01:15,000 --> 01:01:16,280
Don't move. This one.

1009
01:01:53,600 --> 01:01:54,560
Master Wang.

1010
01:01:55,360 --> 01:01:56,440
Master Wang.

1011
01:01:56,520 --> 01:01:57,480
Over here.

1012
01:01:58,040 --> 01:01:59,280
Something's happened, Master Wang.

1013
01:01:59,360 --> 01:02:00,280
What is it?

1014
01:02:00,760 --> 01:02:01,600
Your wife called.

1015
01:02:01,680 --> 01:02:03,520
Said your son was taken by the police.

1016
01:02:06,160 --> 01:02:08,360
(Hualin Municipal Public Security Bureau)

1017
01:02:08,440 --> 01:02:13,800
(The People's Police Serve the People)

1018
01:02:34,280 --> 01:02:35,360
What's going on?

1019
01:02:36,720 --> 01:02:38,360
I'm asking you what's going on.

1020
01:02:38,440 --> 01:02:40,640
Master Wang, don't panic yet.

1021
01:02:41,360 --> 01:02:42,320
There's a case.

1022
01:02:42,400 --> 01:02:43,960
We brought him in to ask some questions.

1023
01:02:44,040 --> 01:02:45,880
We're done. Take him home.

1024
01:02:47,080 --> 01:02:48,080
What case?

1025
01:02:48,800 --> 01:02:49,720
What case?

1026
01:02:50,280 --> 01:02:51,440
What case?

1027
01:02:54,760 --> 01:02:55,840
Stay there.

1028
01:02:56,680 --> 01:02:58,080
Did I say you could go?

1029
01:02:59,320 --> 01:03:01,640
Um... is Captain Ma in?

1030
01:03:01,720 --> 01:03:02,880
Go on over.

1031
01:03:03,520 --> 01:03:04,840
Keep an eye on him for me.

1032
01:03:07,440 --> 01:03:08,800
Captain Ma.

1033
01:03:08,880 --> 01:03:10,240
I thought you weren't in.

1034
01:03:10,320 --> 01:03:12,000
Seeing you puts me at ease.

1035
01:03:14,480 --> 01:03:17,160
What's happened to my Yang'er, Captain Ma?

1036
01:03:27,040 --> 01:03:28,240
Wang Yang is your son?

1037
01:03:28,960 --> 01:03:30,000
That's right.

1038
01:03:31,440 --> 01:03:34,120
He has a girlfriend named Shen Mo. You knew?

1039
01:03:35,480 --> 01:03:36,520
Shen Mo?

1040
01:03:37,520 --> 01:03:39,200
I didn't know he had a girlfriend.

1041
01:03:39,880 --> 01:03:41,000
You two go home and talk it over.

1042
01:03:41,080 --> 01:03:42,200
I'm done asking.

1043
01:03:42,760 --> 01:03:45,280
Tell Wang Yang he's not to leave Hualin for now.

1044
01:03:45,840 --> 01:03:47,720
We may question him anytime.

1045
01:03:52,240 --> 01:03:53,080
Okay.

1046
01:03:55,760 --> 01:03:56,800
Captain Ma.

1047
01:03:58,240 --> 01:04:00,320
-I did some canvassing...
-Master Wang.

1048
01:04:02,400 --> 01:04:03,920
Don't come to the bureau without cause.

1049
01:04:05,160 --> 01:04:07,760
And stop fretting over this case.

1050
01:04:08,760 --> 01:04:10,000
Just drive your train.

1051
01:04:13,840 --> 01:04:15,720
Aren't I your Watson?

1052
01:04:16,880 --> 01:04:18,360
Read fewer novels.

1053
01:04:20,720 --> 01:04:21,880
I like Chandler.

1054
01:04:22,560 --> 01:04:24,760
Guodong, see Master Wang out.

1055
01:04:25,680 --> 01:04:27,240
What... what-dler?

1056
01:04:27,320 --> 01:04:28,560
Master Wang.

1057
01:04:28,640 --> 01:04:29,880
Get going.

1058
01:04:29,960 --> 01:04:30,960
Okay.

1059
01:04:33,360 --> 01:04:34,280
Captain Ma, I...

1060
01:04:35,480 --> 01:04:36,480
Okay.

1061
01:05:01,960 --> 01:05:03,440
You just had to stir up trouble.

1062
01:05:04,360 --> 01:05:05,880
A girlfriend pops up out of nowhere.

1063
01:05:06,480 --> 01:05:08,200
What's with this girl?

1064
01:05:10,040 --> 01:05:12,080
I told the police everything I should.

1065
01:05:13,240 --> 01:05:14,840
She's dead, you know?

1066
01:05:16,520 --> 01:05:19,240
I told you not to work at that dump.

1067
01:05:19,320 --> 01:05:20,720
You boasted you just had to go.

1068
01:05:22,240 --> 01:05:23,320
Just wait.

1069
01:05:24,280 --> 01:05:25,840
When we're home, I'm locking you up.

1070
01:05:26,920 --> 01:05:28,360
Once this is all cleared up,

1071
01:05:28,880 --> 01:05:30,160
then I'll let you downstairs.

1072
01:05:35,920 --> 01:05:37,280
Stop.

1073
01:05:40,560 --> 01:05:42,680
Will running solve anything?

1074
01:05:43,360 --> 01:05:45,680
Just talk it out—isn't that enough?

1075
01:06:03,880 --> 01:06:04,880
Where's Yang'er?

1076
01:06:05,400 --> 01:06:06,400
Why isn't Yang'er back?

1077
01:06:06,480 --> 01:06:09,120
He'll be back soon, right behind me.

1078
01:06:09,640 --> 01:06:10,720
What did the police say?

1079
01:06:10,800 --> 01:06:12,280
Nothing much. It's fine.

1080
01:06:12,880 --> 01:06:14,720
If it's nothing, why'd they take him?

1081
01:06:15,360 --> 01:06:17,840
You... wait up, I'm talking to you.

1082
01:06:21,880 --> 01:06:23,240
No—I called you

1083
01:06:23,320 --> 01:06:25,080
just to pick up our son, right?

1084
01:06:25,160 --> 01:06:27,120
So where did you take him?

1085
01:06:27,200 --> 01:06:28,600
God, my heart's been pounding like crazy.

1086
01:06:28,680 --> 01:06:30,280
Is Yang'er really okay?

1087
01:06:30,360 --> 01:06:31,680
Don't lie to me.

1088
01:06:32,680 --> 01:06:34,800
He's my own son. Would I let him get hurt?

1089
01:06:34,880 --> 01:06:36,280
Then when's he coming back?

1090
01:06:36,360 --> 01:06:37,400
Stop following me.

1091
01:06:37,480 --> 01:06:39,360
My head's buzzing. I'll lie down a bit.

1092
01:06:41,280 --> 01:06:43,120
God, mine's buzzing too.

1093
01:07:12,440 --> 01:07:15,400
(Forensics Lab)

1094
01:07:15,480 --> 01:07:16,520
That's enough.

1095
01:07:20,560 --> 01:07:22,560
Captain Ma, this is Shen Mo's family.

1096
01:07:22,640 --> 01:07:24,320
They came from Songhe for the identification.

1097
01:07:24,400 --> 01:07:26,880
This is our sub-bureau's Criminal Police captain, Ma Desheng.

1098
01:07:26,960 --> 01:07:27,920
Hello.

1099
01:07:28,920 --> 01:07:30,360
Captain Ma.

1100
01:07:30,440 --> 01:07:32,680
My hometown is Hualin too.

1101
01:07:33,480 --> 01:07:36,680
I worked here in Hualin years ago.

1102
01:07:36,760 --> 01:07:39,840
I know some leaders in your police system quite well.

1103
01:07:41,000 --> 01:07:42,200
You done?

1104
01:07:42,280 --> 01:07:44,040
Li Qun, take these two to the office first.

1105
01:07:44,720 --> 01:07:45,680
Let's go.

1106
01:07:46,320 --> 01:07:47,440
Anything else?

1107
01:07:47,520 --> 01:07:49,760
Well, the case is still under investigation.

1108
01:07:49,840 --> 01:07:52,160
We need to ask about Shen Mo's recent situation.

1109
01:07:53,240 --> 01:07:54,400
Here's the thing.

1110
01:07:54,480 --> 01:07:56,160
I've already bought my return ticket.

1111
01:07:56,240 --> 01:07:58,920
You know trains wait for no one.

1112
01:07:59,000 --> 01:08:02,400
I have a lot waiting for me back in Songhe.

1113
01:08:02,480 --> 01:08:04,320
We can't exactly chat on the train, can we?

1114
01:08:05,240 --> 01:08:06,280
We're all busy.

1115
01:08:08,200 --> 01:08:09,160
Fine.

1116
01:08:09,240 --> 01:08:11,320
Then we'll cooperate.

1117
01:08:12,880 --> 01:08:14,240
Stop crying.

1118
01:08:17,040 --> 01:08:18,120
Let's go.

1119
01:08:30,560 --> 01:08:31,479
Captain Ma.

1120
01:08:31,560 --> 01:08:33,399
Why does he seem so off to me?

1121
01:08:33,960 --> 01:08:34,920
Off how?

1122
01:08:35,479 --> 01:08:37,439
To me, you two actually look quite alike.

1123
01:08:38,040 --> 01:08:39,240
What nonsense.

1124
01:08:39,840 --> 01:08:42,319
I mean, he doesn't look like her real dad.

1125
01:08:42,399 --> 01:08:43,720
He's not her real dad.

1126
01:08:43,800 --> 01:08:44,920
He's her uncle.

1127
01:08:45,479 --> 01:08:47,160
He adopted Shen Mo.

1128
01:08:47,880 --> 01:08:50,640
(The People's Police Serve the People)

1129
01:08:54,399 --> 01:08:55,560
Come here a sec.

1130
01:08:57,279 --> 01:08:58,560
Look.

1131
01:08:58,640 --> 01:08:59,840
You've got sharp eyes.

1132
01:08:59,920 --> 01:09:02,200
Check the thermos on this nightstand for me.

1133
01:09:02,279 --> 01:09:03,800
There are two characters on it.

1134
01:09:03,880 --> 01:09:05,359
What's this second character?

1135
01:09:06,520 --> 01:09:08,359
The paint's worn off the bottle.

1136
01:09:08,439 --> 01:09:10,800
Duh—why else would I ask you?

1137
01:09:13,720 --> 01:09:14,720
"Hui."

1138
01:09:14,800 --> 01:09:15,760
The character "hui."

1139
01:09:16,319 --> 01:09:17,279
Let's see.

1140
01:09:19,720 --> 01:09:21,840
Captain Ma, Chief Zhu called a meeting.

1141
01:09:24,080 --> 01:09:25,720
Calling a meeting now of all times.

1142
01:09:27,720 --> 01:09:28,600
Here.

1143
01:09:28,680 --> 01:09:29,880
Save it for when I'm back.

1144
01:09:29,960 --> 01:09:31,720
Let me get a sip—so thirsty.

1145
01:09:32,240 --> 01:09:33,439
There's no water here.

1146
01:09:33,520 --> 01:09:34,560
Hurry...

1147
01:10:01,840 --> 01:10:02,840
Chief Zhu.

1148
01:10:02,920 --> 01:10:03,880
Sit.

1149
01:10:09,120 --> 01:10:10,240
Chief Zhu.

1150
01:10:11,880 --> 01:10:14,640
This so-called Hong Kong businessman is really from Zhanjiang, Guangdong.

1151
01:10:14,720 --> 01:10:16,080
He registered a company in Hong Kong.

1152
01:10:16,560 --> 01:10:17,960
On the 5th, he spoke with his driver by phone.

1153
01:10:18,880 --> 01:10:20,400
Then he became unreachable.

1154
01:10:20,480 --> 01:10:23,120
Before vanishing, he received an 800,000-yuan money order from Hualin Steel.

1155
01:10:23,200 --> 01:10:25,280
The bank says someone tried to cash it.

1156
01:10:25,360 --> 01:10:28,440
So we suspect this may not be a simple economic case.

1157
01:10:29,840 --> 01:10:32,080
Are you across this, Ma Desheng?

1158
01:10:34,200 --> 01:10:36,280
What kind of captain are you?

1159
01:10:36,360 --> 01:10:37,840
None of us have been idle.

1160
01:10:37,920 --> 01:10:39,640
I want results.

1161
01:10:40,200 --> 01:10:41,680
Drop the dismemberment case.

1162
01:10:41,760 --> 01:10:42,800
Hand it to the main squad.

1163
01:10:42,880 --> 01:10:44,520
You all now go all-out

1164
01:10:44,600 --> 01:10:46,560
on the cash-withdrawal lead.

1165
01:10:47,080 --> 01:10:49,200
First find out who tried to cash that money.

1166
01:10:49,280 --> 01:10:50,840
Find...

1167
01:10:50,920 --> 01:10:52,000
Definitely on it.

1168
01:10:52,080 --> 01:10:53,240
I never said I wouldn't investigate.

1169
01:10:53,320 --> 01:10:55,600
Give me two days—till I'm back from Songhe.

1170
01:10:55,680 --> 01:10:57,240
Why Songhe?

1171
01:10:57,320 --> 01:11:00,360
I suspect the guy who took Shen Mo's nudes and wrote the anonymous letter

1172
01:11:00,440 --> 01:11:02,160
had an unusual relationship with her.

1173
01:11:02,240 --> 01:11:04,280
I'm heading to Songhe right away—alone.

1174
01:11:04,360 --> 01:11:05,960
I'll question her family thoroughly.

1175
01:11:06,040 --> 01:11:08,320
Ma Desheng, do you not understand what I'm saying?

1176
01:11:08,400 --> 01:11:09,800
I can't work on anything else right now.

1177
01:11:10,520 --> 01:11:12,320
Those body parts are just lying there.

1178
01:11:13,000 --> 01:11:14,040
We're this close to a lead.

1179
01:11:14,120 --> 01:11:15,480
What if the guy really runs?

1180
01:11:15,560 --> 01:11:17,720
Ma Desheng, you are a police officer.

1181
01:11:17,800 --> 01:11:20,640
You must do your duty on every case.

1182
01:11:20,720 --> 01:11:22,000
I am a cop—

1183
01:11:22,080 --> 01:11:23,480
and this is a homicide.

1184
01:11:25,000 --> 01:11:25,960
Chief Zhu.

1185
01:11:26,600 --> 01:11:29,680
I have some thoughts on the missing businessman.

1186
01:11:30,280 --> 01:11:34,040
How about I watch the withdrawal lead for Captain Ma for two days?

1187
01:11:34,120 --> 01:11:35,960
Stay out of it. This doesn't concern you.

1188
01:11:36,040 --> 01:11:37,240
How does it not?

1189
01:11:37,320 --> 01:11:38,840
He's a cop too.

1190
01:11:49,200 --> 01:11:56,120
(The People's Police Serve the People)

1191
01:12:01,280 --> 01:12:02,240
The bag.

1192
01:12:06,200 --> 01:12:08,120
Driving there alone this late?

1193
01:12:08,200 --> 01:12:10,000
What? You want to come along?

1194
01:12:10,080 --> 01:12:11,720
Get in. I'll drive you.

1195
01:12:11,800 --> 01:12:13,680
Better help Li Qun with the money order.

1196
01:12:13,760 --> 01:12:16,080
I'll be fine—back first thing tomorrow.

1197
01:12:16,880 --> 01:12:19,200
Don't keep bringing him up to me.

1198
01:12:19,280 --> 01:12:20,760
You saw that just now, right?

1199
01:12:21,280 --> 01:12:22,560
Him, offering opinions.

1200
01:12:22,640 --> 01:12:23,600
Is it his place?

1201
01:12:23,680 --> 01:12:25,040
The nerve of him.

1202
01:12:25,120 --> 01:12:26,600
He did take some heat off me.

1203
01:12:26,680 --> 01:12:28,200
Alright, I'm off.

1204
01:12:30,880 --> 01:12:31,760
Got a smoke?

1205
01:12:31,840 --> 01:12:33,520
What? Not quitting anymore?

1206
01:12:36,600 --> 01:12:37,840
Forget it.

